1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,779
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,900
In this lesson, we will plan
coverage and keep dispatch aligned.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,729
A paper duty schedule and a dispatch
roster can drift apart, especially

4
00:00:10,729 --> 00:00:12,890
when members sign up or trade shifts.

5
00:00:13,319 --> 00:00:16,489
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,489 --> 00:00:18,420
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:23,880
A career department sets up A, B and C
shifts, and a volunteer department uses

8
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:26,090
shift sign-ups for weekend duty crews.

9
00:00:26,549 --> 00:00:30,589
Shifts show who is on duty and can
drive dispatch, so calls page the

10
00:00:30,589 --> 00:00:32,339
people who are actually working.

11
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,170
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:38,410
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,209
Shifts.

14
00:00:39,589 --> 00:00:42,300
Shift schedules, sign-ups and trades.

15
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:46,119
Create your shifts, assign
groups and members, and decide

16
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:47,980
whether dispatch follows shifts.

17
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:50,660
Availability also depends on Shifts.

18
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:53,219
Check access in the target department.

19
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,040
Calendar.

20
00:00:54,409 --> 00:00:57,979
The department calendar for
meetings, events and training nights.

21
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:00,599
Add recurring meetings
and training nights.

22
00:01:00,979 --> 00:01:03,389
Availability also depends on Calendar.

23
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:05,979
Check access in the target department.

24
00:01:06,109 --> 00:01:07,420
New Calendar Event.

25
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,869
Add an event to the department calendar.

26
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:13,290
Have your rotation or duty
schedule, and decide whether

27
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:15,050
dispatch should follow shifts.

28
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:17,739
Availability also depends on Calendar.

29
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:20,380
Check access in the target department.

30
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:20,959
Workshifts.

31
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:23,670
Repeating work schedules for staff.

32
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:27,059
Have your rotation or duty
schedule, and decide whether

33
00:01:27,059 --> 00:01:28,750
dispatch should follow shifts.

34
00:01:29,139 --> 00:01:31,540
Availability also depends on Shifts.

35
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:34,049
Check access in the target department.

36
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,919
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

37
00:01:37,410 --> 00:01:38,019
Step 1.

38
00:01:38,529 --> 00:01:42,330
Create an assigned or signup shift
with groups and staffing needs.

39
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,510
Step 2.

40
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:47,399
Have demo members sign up or
complete a trade where supported.

41
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,620
Step 3.

42
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:53,690
Review whether dispatch follows groups or
shifts and confirm the calendar time zone.

43
00:01:53,879 --> 00:01:55,410
Now verify the result.

44
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,640
Compare the scheduled roster
with the people dispatch would

45
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,289
include at the selected time.

46
00:02:00,729 --> 00:02:03,550
Check trade completion and
the visible duty coverage.

47
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:07,650
A common problem to watch
for: A calendar event is not

48
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:09,390
automatically a duty assignment.

49
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:13,350
Shift dispatch behavior must be
reviewed on Dispatch Settings.

50
00:02:13,549 --> 00:02:15,179
Your practice task is simple.

51
00:02:15,619 --> 00:02:18,969
Schedule a weekend duty crew,
change one assignment, and

52
00:02:18,969 --> 00:02:20,770
verify the expected roster.

53
00:02:21,179 --> 00:02:23,900
Track unfilled slots
and unresolved trades.

54
00:02:24,249 --> 00:02:28,129
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

55
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:31,989
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
